  "articleBody": "When you're dealing with interior damage, it's easy to make a few missteps that can end up costing you more time and money. One of the biggest mistakes is choosing a repair service based solely on the lowest price. While budget is important, the cheapest option might not provide the quality or durability you need. Always get a written estimate too; skipping this can lead to unexpected costs down the line. Another common pitfall is not confirming warranty terms for the repair. You want to know what's covered if something doesn't hold up. And here's a big one: failing to ask if the repair will match the original texture and color. You don't want a perfectly repaired spot that sticks out like a sore thumb. For instance, if you have custom tile, you need someone who can truly match that aesthetic. If you're in the greater Denver area and have interior damage, we pride ourselves on clear communication and making sure you understand what to expect. We want you to be satisfied with our work, so don't hesitate to ask all your questions upfront. Reach out to us for a reliable estimate and service.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
